<p dir=3D"auto">In React, component names must start with a capital letter =
because of how JSX distinguishes between HTML elements and React components=
:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Reasons:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. JSX Compilation Behavior:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>&lt;component /&gt;</code> =E2=86=92 compiles to React.createElem=
ent('component') (treated as HTML tag string)</li>
<li><code>&lt;Component /&gt;</code> =E2=86=92 compiles to React.createElem=
ent(Component) (treated as React component)</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Built-in vs Custom Components:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Lowercase names refer to built-in HTML elements like <code>&lt;div&gt;<=
/code>, <code>&lt;span&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;button&gt;</code></li>
<li>Capitalized names refer to custom React components you've defined or im=
ported</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>3. Exception:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Lowercase with dot notation works: <code>&lt;obj.component =
/&gt;</code> compiles to <code>React.createElement(obj.component)</code></p=
>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">//  Wrong - React trea=
ts this as HTML &lt;mybutton&gt; tag</span>
<span class=3D"pl-k">function</span> <span class=3D"pl-en">myButton</span><=
span class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">)</span> <span class=
=3D"pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class=3D"pl-k">return</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">&lt;</span><span=
 class=3D"pl-s1">button</span><span class=3D"pl-c1">&gt;</span>Click me<spa=
n class=3D"pl-kos">&lt;/</span><span class=3D"pl-s1">button</span><span cla=
ss=3D"pl-c1">&gt;</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">;</span>
<span class=3D"pl-kos">}</span>

<span class=3D"pl-c">// Using it: &lt;myButton /&gt; // Won\'t work as expe=
cted</span>

<span class=3D"pl-c">//  Correct - React treats this as a component</span>
<span class=3D"pl-k">function</span> <span class=3D"pl-v">MyButton</span><s=
pan class=3D"pl-kos">(</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">)</span> <span class=3D=
"pl-kos">{</span>
  <span class=3D"pl-k">return</span> <span class=3D"pl-c1">&lt;</span><span=
