<p dir=3D"auto">React Fragments are a way to group multiple elements withou=
t adding an extra node to the browser's DOM.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Why use Fragments?</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Avoid extra DOM nodes that can affect styling and layout</li>
<li>Cleaner DOM structure</li>
<li>Better performance (fewer nodes to render)</li>
<li>Satisfy React's requirement that components return a single element</li=
>
<li>Adding a <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> inside elements like <code>&lt;table&=
gt;</code>, <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code>, or <code>&lt;ul&gt;</code> can break t=
he browser's layout rules.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">// Long syntax</span>
<span class=3D"pl-k">import</span> <span class=3D"pl-v">React</span><span c=
lass=3D"pl-kos">,</span> <span class=3D"pl-kos">{</span> <span class=3D"pl-=
v">Fragment</span> <span class=3D"pl-kos">}</span> <span class=3D"pl-k">fro=
m</span> <span class=3D"pl-s">'react'</span><span class=3D"pl-kos">;</span>

<span class=3D"pl-k">function</span> <span class=3D"pl-v">MyComponent</span=
