<p dir=3D"auto">In React, calling setState() on an unmounted component shou=
ld be avoided primarily because it signals a potential memory leak in your =
application.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The component retains references in memory even after unmou=
nting, preventing garbage collection. Subscriptions, timers, or async opera=
tions holding references to the component keep it alive unnecessarily</p>
