<p dir=3D"auto">Compound Components is an advanced React design pattern whe=
re multiple components work together to form a cohesive unit while sharing =
an implicit state.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How It Works:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Compound components use React's lower-level APIs:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>React.Children.map()</code> - to iterate over children</li>
<li><code>React.cloneElement()</code> - to pass implicit props/state to chi=
ldren</li>
<li><code>Context API</code> (modern approach) - to share state</li>
</ul>
