<p dir=3D"auto">In React.js, the most reliable way to set a timer that upda=
tes every second is by using the <code>useEffect()</code> and <code>useStat=
e()</code> hooks together.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Core Implementation:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">To ensure your timer starts correctly and doesn't cause mem=
ory leaks, follow these three steps:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>State</strong>: Store the timer value in a useState variable.</=
li>
<li><strong>Interval</strong>: Create the timer using setInterval inside a =
useEffect hook with an empty dependency array (<code>[]</code>) so it only =
starts once when the component mounts.</li>
<li><strong>Cleanup</strong>: Return a function that calls clearInterval to=
 stop the timer when the component is removed (unmounted).</li>
</ul>
