<p dir=3D"auto">In React, the <code>render()</code> function is a core life=
cycle method used primarily in class components to define the visual struct=
ure of the user interface (UI). It acts as a "blueprint" that tells React w=
hat elements should appear on the screen based on the component's current d=
ata</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key purposes:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Returns UI elements</strong> - Displays specified HTML/JSX insi=
de a DOM element</li>
<li><strong>Reads props and state</strong> - Accesses component data to det=
ermine what to render</li>
<li><strong>Pure function</strong> - Cannot modify state or cause side effe=
cts (like HTTP requests)</li>
<li><strong>Required method</strong> - Every class component must have a re=
nder() method</li>
</ul>
