<p dir=3D"auto">When the <code>key</code> changes, React recognizes it as a=
 different component and will:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Unmount the old instance</li>
<li>Create a new instance from scratch</li>
<li>Call the constructor again</li>
<li>Go through the full component lifecycle</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto">This is why constructors are called only once per component=
 instance - React optimizes by reusing instances when possible, unless you =
explicitly signal otherwise with the key prop.</p>
