<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>defaultProps</strong> is a React component prop=
erty that allows you to set default values for the props argument. If the p=
rop property is passed, it will be changed.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">The <code>defaultProps</code> can be defined as a property =
on the component class itself to set the default props for the class. <code=
>defaultProps</code> is used for <strong>undefined</strong> props, not for =
<strong>null</strong> props.</p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/**</span>
