<p dir=3D"auto">You can create a Higher Order Component (HOC) using render =
props by combining the two patterns: the HOC returns a component that uses =
a render prop to share logic or state with the wrapped component. Here is h=
ow you do it:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Define a function (the HOC) that takes a component as an argument.</li>
<li>Inside, return a new component that renders the original component, pas=
sing it data or methods via props.</li>
<li>Use a render prop internally to provide the shared logic or state.</li>
</ul>
