<p dir=3D"auto"><code>React.createElement</code> is used to create a new Re=
act element from scratch. It's what JSX compiles to under the hood. It is u=
sed when you want to define what to render for the first time.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>React.cloneElement</code> is used to clone and return=
 a copy of an existing React element, with new props or children merged in.=
 It's useful when you want to take an existing element (often passed as chi=
ldren) and add or override some props before rendering.</p>
