<p dir=3D"auto">In React, the <code>setState()</code> method is used to upd=
ate the state of a class component. When you call <code>setState()</code>, =
React schedules a re-render of the component with the new state values. Thi=
s allows your UI to update in response to user actions or other events. <co=
de>setState()</code> is asynchronous and can accept either an object with u=
pdated state values or a function that returns the new state based on the p=
revious state.</p>
