<p dir=3D"auto">The setState() will always lead to a re-render unless <code=
>shouldComponentUpdate()</code> returns <strong>false</strong>. To avoid un=
necessary renders, calling setState() only when the new state differs from =
the previous state makes sense and can avoid calling setState() in an infin=
ite loop within certain lifecycle methods like <code>componentDidUpdate()</=
code>.</p>
