<p dir=3D"auto">React components automatically re-render whenever there is =
a change in their state or props. A simple update of the state, from anywhe=
re in the code, causes all the User Interface (UI) elements to be re-render=
ed automatically.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">However, there may be cases where the render() method depen=
ds on some other data. After the initial mounting of components, a re-rende=
r will occur.</p>
