<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Differences:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th></th>
<th><code>useCallback</code></th>
<th><code>useMemo</code></th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Returns</td>
<td>The memoized <strong>function</strong></td>
<td>The memoized <strong>value</strong> (result of calling the function)</t=
d>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Purpose</td>
<td>Stable function reference for props/deps</td>
<td>Cache expensive computation</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Example use</td>
<td>Event handlers, callbacks passed to <code>React.memo</code> components<=
/td>
<td>Filtered lists, derived data, sorted arrays</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Mental model</td>
<td><code>useCallback(fn, deps)</code> =E2=89=A1 <code>useMemo(() =3D&gt; f=
n, deps)</code></td>
<td>Calls fn, caches result</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When NOT to use them:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Don't use either hook for cheap computations =E2=80=94 the memoization =
overhead can cost more than the saved work.</li>
<li>Don't use <code>useCallback</code> if the child component isn't wrapped=
 in <code>React.memo</code> =E2=80=94 the memoized callback won't prevent r=
e-renders.</li>
<li>Premature optimization is a code smell. Profile first with React DevToo=
ls Profiler, then optimize.</li>
</ul>
