<p dir=3D"auto">If your component renders the same result given the same pr=
ops, you can wrap it in a call to <code>React.memo</code> for a performance=
 boost in some cases by memoizing the result. This means that React will sk=
ip rendering the component, and reuse the last rendered result.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><code>React.memo</code> only checks for prop changes. If yo=
ur function component wrapped in <code>React.memo</code> has a <code>useSta=
te</code>, <code>useReducer</code> or <code>useContext</code> Hook in its i=
mplementation, it will still rerender when state or context change.</p>
