<p dir=3D"auto"><code>useDeferredValue()</code> is a React Hook (introduced=
 in React 18) that lets you defer re-rendering a <strong>non-urgent part of=
 the UI</strong>. You pass it a value, and React will keep showing the old =
value while it prepares the updated expensive render in the background.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">It is similar to <code>useTransition()</code> but works on =
values rather than on the state-setter call =E2=80=94 useful when you don't=
 control the state update that triggers the expensive render (e.g., a value=
 comes from a prop or external store).</p>
