<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Why do these rules exist?</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">React relies on the <strong>call order</strong> of Hooks to=
 associate state with the correct component instance. On every render, Reac=
t expects the same number of Hooks to be called in the same sequence. If yo=
u skip a Hook call (due to a condition), React loses track of which state c=
orresponds to which Hook.</p>
