<p dir=3D"auto">In React, you pass an event handler to a component by defin=
ing a function in the parent and passing it as a <strong>prop</strong> to t=
he child component. The child then "plugs" that prop into a standard HTML e=
vent attribute like <code>onClick</code>.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Pattern</strong>:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Define the handler in the parent</li>
<li>Pass it as a prop to the child</li>
<li>The child attaches it to a DOM element</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c">/**</span>
<span class=3D"pl-c"> * Pass an event handler to a component</span>
