<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Strategy comparison:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Strategy</th>
<th>Best for</th>
<th>Complexity</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Virtualization</td>
<td>Any large list (1k+ items visible)</td>
<td>Medium</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Pagination</td>
<td>Tabular data, server-side data</td>
<td>Low</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Infinite scroll</td>
<td>Social feeds, search results</td>
<td>Medium</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Memoization</td>
<td>Preventing unnecessary re-renders</td>
<td>Low</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto">For most apps: <strong>virtualize</strong> if all data is i=
n memory (e.g. a local dataset), <strong>paginate or infinite-scroll</stron=
g> if data is fetched from a server.</p>
