<p dir=3D"auto">In a controlled component, form data is handled by a React =
component. The alternative is uncontrolled components, where form data is h=
andled by the DOM itself.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Controlled Components:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In a controlled component, the form data is handled by the =
state within the component. The state within the component serves as "the s=
ingle source of truth" for the input elements that are rendered by the comp=
onent.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Uncontrolled Components:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Uncontrolled components act more like traditional HTML form=
 elements. The data for each input element is stored in the DOM, not in the=
 component. Instead of writing an event handler for all of your state updat=
es, It uses <code>ref</code> to retrieve values from the DOM. <code>Refs</c=
ode> provide a way to access DOM nodes or React elements created in the ren=
der method.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
