<p dir=3D"auto">React Components can add styling in the following ways:</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Inline Styles:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Inline styles are applied directly to elements using the st=
yle attribute. In React, this attribute accepts a JavaScript object rather =
than a string.</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>CamelCase Keys:</strong> CSS properties with hyphens (e.g., bac=
kground-color) must be written in camelCase (e.g., backgroundColor).</li>
<li><strong>Syntax:</strong> Use double curly braces <code>{{ }}</code>=E2=
=80=94the outer pair for JSX expression and the inner for the object litera=
l.</li>
<li><strong>Use Case:</strong> Best for dynamic, state-based styles (like a=
