<p dir=3D"auto">React router enables the navigation among views of various =
components in a React Application, allows changing the browser URL, and kee=
ps the UI in sync with the URL. It has a simple API with powerful features =
like lazy loading, dynamic route matching, and location transition handling=
.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Core components (v7):</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>BrowserRouter:</strong>	Parent wrapper; uses HTML5 History API =
to sync UI with URL</li>
<li><strong>Routes:</strong>	Container for all Route definitions; matches t=
he best route</li>
<li><strong>Route:</strong>	Maps a URL path to a component</li>
<li><strong>Link / NavLink:</strong>	Declarative navigation; NavLink adds a=
ctive styling</li>
</ul>
