<p dir=3D"auto">React Router is a high-level, React-specific routing librar=
y built <strong>on top of</strong> the low-level <code>history</code> libra=
ry. While the <code>history</code> library handles raw browser history mani=
pulation, React Router adds declarative routing, component rendering, and R=
eact hooks on top of it.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Differences:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th><code>history</code> library</th>
<th>React Router v7</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Level</td>
<td>Low-level</td>
<td>High-level</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>React awareness</td>
<td>None</td>
<td>React-specific</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Navigation</td>
<td><code>history.push('/path')</code></td>
<td><code>useNavigate()</code> hook</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Location access</td>
<td><code>history.location</code></td>
<td><code>useLocation()</code> hook</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>URL params</td>
<td>Manual</td>
<td><code>useParams()</code> hook</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>UI sync</td>
<td>Manual</td>
<td>Automatic</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
