<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Differences</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>JSON Parsing</strong>: <code>fetch()</code> require=
s manual parsing (<code>.json()</code>), whereas Axios returns the parsed d=
ata in response.data.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Error Detection</strong>: <code>fetch()</code> requ=
ires checking <code>response.ok</code>, while Axios automatically triggers =
the catch block for <code>non-2xx</code> status codes.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Best Practices:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Keep API calls in <code>useEffect</code> (or a custom hook).</li>
<li>Always handle loading, error, and cleanup.</li>
<li>Use stable keys while rendering list data.</li>
<li>For larger apps, consider <strong>React Query</strong> or <strong>SWR</=
strong> for caching/retries.</li>
</ul>
