<p dir=3D"auto">Caching in React is typically handled through three distinc=
t layers: Memoization (internal logic), Data Fetching (network requests), a=
nd Browser/Persistent Storage (long-term data)</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. In-Component Memoization</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">These built-in hooks prevent expensive calculations or comp=
onent re-renders when inputs haven't changed.</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>useMemo</strong>: Caches the result of a calculation. Use it fo=
r heavy data processing to avoid recalculating on every render.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
