<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>ContextType</strong> property on a <strong>clas=
s component</strong> can be assigned a Context object created by <code>Reac=
t.createContext()</code> method. This property lets you consume the nearest=
 current value of the context using <code>this.context</code>. We can acces=
s <code>this.context</code> in any lifecycle method including the render fu=
nctions.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Concept:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Create a context with <code>React.createContext(defaultValue)</code>.</=
li>
<li>Wrap part of the tree with Provider and pass value.</li>
<li>In a class component, assign static <code>contextType =3D MyContext</co=
de>.</li>
<li>Access context anywhere in the class with <code>this.context</code> (re=
nder and lifecycle methods).</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Example:</strong></p>
