<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Higher Order Components (HOCs)</strong> are advance=
d React patterns where a function takes a component and returns a new enhan=
ced component with additional props or functionality.</p>
<p align=3D"center" dir=3D"auto">
  <a target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer" href=3D"https://github.c=
om/learning-zone/react-basics/blob/master/assets/Higher-Order-Components.jp=
g"><img src=3D"https://github.com/learning-zone/react-basics/raw/master/ass=
ets/Higher-Order-Components.jpg" alt=3D"Higher Order Components" width=3D"3=
00px" style=3D"max-width: 100%;"></a>
</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Higher-Order Components are not part of the React API. They=
 are the pattern that emerges from React's compositional nature. The compon=
ent transforms props into UI, and a higher-order component converts a compo=
nent into another component. The examples of HOCs are Redux's connect and R=
elay's createContainer.</p>
