<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When to Use Refs:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Managing focus, text selection, or media playback.</li>
<li>Triggering imperative animations.</li>
<li>Integrating non-React libraries (like D3.js or Google Maps) that requir=
e direct access to DOM nodes.</li>
<li>Keeping track of <code>setTimeout</code> or <code>setInterval</code> ID=
s so they can be cleared later.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>When not to use refs:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Should not be used with functional components (they don't have instance=
s).</li>
<li>Not to be used on things that can be done declaratively.</li>
</ul>
