<p dir=3D"auto">Inline <strong>ref callbacks</strong> are not recommended b=
ecause they get called twice on every update:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><strong>Cleanup:</strong> It calls the old function with null to clear =
the previous reference.</li>
<li><strong>Setup:</strong> It calls the new function with the actual DOM e=
lement to set the new reference.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto">This happens because a new function instance is created on =
every render, so React treats it as a different ref each time and must clea=
n up the old one before assigning the new one.</p>
