<p dir=3D"auto">We pass our ref down to <code>&lt;TextInput ref=3D{inputRef=
}&gt;</code> by specifying it as a JSX attribute. React then forwards the <=
code>ref</code> to the <code>forwardRef()</code> function as a second argum=
ent. Next, We forward this <code>ref</code> argument down to <code>&lt;inpu=
t ref=3D{ref}&gt;</code>. The value of the DOM node can now be accessed at =
<code>inputRef.current</code>.</p>
