<p dir=3D"auto">Error boundaries are React components that catch JavaScript=
 errors anywhere in their child component tree, log those errors, and displ=
ay a fallback UI instead of the component tree that crashed. Error boundari=
es catch errors during rendering, in lifecycle methods, and in constructors=
 of the whole tree below them.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key methods:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li><code>static getDerivedStateFromError()</code>	Update state to render f=
allback UI</li>
<li><code>componentDidCatch()</code>	Log error info to a reporting service<=
/li>
<li><code>render()</code>	Render children or fallback UI</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Syntax:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-c1">&lt;</span><span clas=
