<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Differences:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In React, the primary difference is that Error Boundaries a=
re for declarative code (the UI structure), while <code>try-catch</code> is=
 for imperative code (logical steps or actions). If there's an error, Error=
 Boundaries trigger a fallback UI for the entire component subtree, whereas=
 <code>try...catch</code> catches errors within specific code execution pat=
hs.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Note:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><em>Error Boundaries cannot catch errors in event handlers =
=E2=80=94 you must use <code>try...catch</code> for those.</em></p>
