<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Two Main Panels:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. Components Tab:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Displays the full React component tree for the current page=
. You can:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Select any component to inspect its current <code>props</code>, <code>s=
tate</code>, <code>context</code>, and <code>hooks</code>.</li>
<li>Edit props and state values live in the browser to test different scena=
rios without changing code.</li>
<li>Highlight components in the page by hovering over them in the tree.</li=
>
<li>Click the <code>&lt;&gt;</code> icon to jump directly to the component'=
s source code.</li>
<li>Filter the tree to hide DOM elements or specific component types.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>2. Profiler Tab:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Records a performance profile of your React app to identify=
 re-render bottlenecks. You can:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Record interactions and see which components rendered, how long each re=
nder took, and why it re-rendered.</li>
<li>View a <strong>Flamegraph</strong> (time breakdown per component) or a =
<strong>Ranked Chart</strong> (components sorted by render time).</li>
<li>Identify components that are re-rendering unnecessarily and should be w=
rapped in <code>React.memo</code>, <code>useMemo</code>, or <code>useCallba=
ck</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Key Features:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th>Description</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><strong>Component tree</strong></td>
<td>Visualize the full hierarchy of React components</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Props/State inspector</strong></td>
<td>View and edit props, state, context, and hooks in real time</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Component search</strong></td>
<td>Quickly find components by name</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Highlight updates</strong></td>
<td>Flash components that re-render (helps spot unnecessary renders)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Profiler</strong></td>
<td>Record and analyze render performance</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Source mapping</strong></td>
<td>Jump to component source code from DevTools</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><strong>Strict Mode badge</strong></td>
<td>See which components are inside <code>&lt;StrictMode&gt;</code></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Highlight Re-renders:</strong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">In the Profiler settings, enable <strong>"Highlight updates=
 when components render"</strong> to visually flash every component that re=
-renders. This is the fastest way to spot components that are re-rendering =
more than necessary.</p>
