<p dir=3D"auto">The <strong>React Profiler</strong> is a built-in tool (ava=
ilable in React DevTools browser extension and programmatically via the <co=
de>&lt;Profiler&gt;</code> component) that measures how often components re=
nder and what their render cost is.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>1. React DevTools Profiler (Browser Extension)</str=
ong></p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Open Chrome/Firefox DevTools =E2=86=92 React tab =E2=86=92 =
Profiler tab:</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Click <strong>Record</strong>, interact with your app, then click <stro=
ng>Stop</strong>.</li>
<li>View a <strong>flame chart</strong> showing which components rendered, =
how long they took, and why they re-rendered.</li>
<li>Look for components that render unnecessarily (appear in every frame de=
spite no prop changes).</li>
</ul>
