<p dir=3D"auto">React <code>StrictMode</code> intentionally invokes certain=
 functions <strong>twice</strong> in development to help you detect side ef=
fects that aren't properly cleaned up. This double-invocation does <strong>=
not</strong> happen in production.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>What gets called twice:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Function component bodies (render phase)</li>
<li><code>useState</code>, <code>useMemo</code>, <code>useReducer</code> in=
itializer functions</li>
<li><code>useEffect</code> setup and cleanup functions (mount =E2=86=92 unm=
ount =E2=86=92 mount)</li>
<li>Class component <code>constructor</code>, <code>render</code>, <code>ge=
tDerivedStateFromProps</code>, <code>shouldComponentUpdate</code></li>
</ul>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Why this matters:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
