<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Mounting</strong> happens once =E2=80=94 when React=
 inserts a component into the DOM for the first time and builds the initial=
 DOM nodes from the component's output.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Rendering</strong> happens every time React calls t=
he component function (or render() method) to get instructions for what the=
 DOM should look like. This occurs on mount and on every subsequent re-rend=
er.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Re-rendering</strong> is when an already-mounted co=
mponent renders again due to a state or prop change =E2=80=94 React calls t=
he component again, diffs the new output against the previous one, and upda=
tes only what changed.</p>
