<p dir=3D"auto">The ESLint plugin ( <strong>eslint-plugin-react-hooks</stro=
ng> ) enforces rules of Hooks to avoid bugs. It assumes that any function s=
tarting with "use" and a capital letter right after it is a Hook. In partic=
ular, the rule enforces that,</p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Calls to Hooks are either inside a PascalCase function (assumed to be a=
 component) or another useSomething function (assumed to be a custom Hook).=
</li>
<li>Hooks are called in the same order on every render.</li>
</ul>
