<p dir=3D"auto">Portals provide a quick and seamless way to render children=
 into a DOM node that exists outside the DOM hierarchy of the parent compon=
ent.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto">Normally, a functional or a class component renders a tree =
of React elements (usually generated from JSX). The React element defines h=
ow the DOM of the parent component should look.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Syntax</strong>:</p>
<div class=3D"highlight highlight-source-js notranslate position-relative o=
verflow-auto" dir=3D"auto"><pre><span class=3D"pl-k">import</span> <span cl=
