<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Server-Side Rendering (SSR)</strong> is the techniq=
ue of rendering a React component tree on the server and sending the result=
ing HTML to the browser. The browser displays the HTML immediately (no blan=
k-screen flicker), then React "hydrates" it =E2=80=94 attaching event liste=
ners and making it interactive.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>How SSR works:</strong></p>
<div class=3D"snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overf=
low-auto"><pre class=3D"notranslate"><code>Client requests URL
       =E2=86=93
Node.js server renders React =E2=86=92 HTML string
       =E2=86=93
Server sends fully-formed HTML to browser
       =E2=86=93
Browser displays HTML (fast First Contentful Paint)
       =E2=86=93
React JavaScript bundle loads
       =E2=86=93
React "hydrates" the HTML (attaches event handlers)
       =E2=86=93
Page is fully interactive
</code></pre><div class=3D"zeroclipboard-container">
