<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Comparison:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Feature</th>
<th>Enzyme</th>
<th>RTL</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Philosophy</td>
<td>Implementation details</td>
<td>User behavior</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Shallow rendering</td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No (full render only)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Access to state</td>
<td>Yes</td>
<td>No (by design)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Query style</td>
<td>CSS selectors, class names</td>
<td>Role, text, label, placeholder</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>React 18 support</td>
<td>Limited / unofficial</td>
<td>Official</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Active maintenance</td>
<td>Minimal</td>
<td>Actively maintained</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recommended for new projects</td>
<td>No</td>
<td>Yes</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Recommendation:</strong></p>
<ul dir=3D"auto">
<li>Use <strong>RTL</strong> for all new React projects. It aligns with bes=
t practices, is actively maintained, and produces more resilient tests.</li=
>
<li><strong>Enzyme</strong> may still be used in legacy codebases but shoul=
d be migrated away from.</li>
</ul>
