<p dir=3D"auto">Cookies can be used for authentication tokens, session IDs,=
 or user preferences, but they must be configured correctly to prevent secu=
rity vulnerabilities.</p>
<p dir=3D"auto"><strong>Secure Cookie Attributes:</strong></p>
<markdown-accessiblity-table data-catalyst=3D""><table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Attribute</th>
<th>Purpose</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td><code>HttpOnly</code></td>
<td>Prevents JavaScript (<code>document.cookie</code>) from accessing the c=
ookie =E2=80=94 mitigates XSS</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Secure</code></td>
<td>Cookie is only sent over HTTPS connections</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>SameSite=3DStrict</code></td>
<td>Cookie not sent on cross-site requests =E2=80=94 prevents CSRF</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>SameSite=3DLax</code></td>
<td>Cookie sent on top-level navigation but not cross-site sub-requests (de=
fault in modern browsers)</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Max-Age</code> / <code>Expires</code></td>
<td>Controls cookie lifetime</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td><code>Path</code></td>
<td>Restricts cookie to a specific URL path</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>
